    "No query-specific gut-wall efflux or intestinal metabolism measurement; L5 records are for tertiary-amine morphinans (naloxone, oxycodone, morphine) and naringenin, not the quaternary query.",
    "No quaternary ammonium analog data in L1-L5.",
    "Ionization behavior at physiological pH is uncertain; the reported neutral fraction (0.97) is inconsistent with the explicit quaternary ammonium charge.",
    "No query-specific formulation, dose, species, or prandial-state data."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted low: the query's permanent quaternary ammonium charge and phenolic morphinan scaffold align with multiple transferable low-F contexts (UK-224,671, estradiol, MK-458, rotigotine, catechins), all below 20%; L2 records reinforce this direction; L5 gut-wall efflux/intestinal metabolism records are for tertiary-amine analogs and do not provide affirmative evidence for query F >= 20%. Confidence remains moderate due to lack of direct query measurement."
}

